From e2e5ea96b2c6b607aeca2afb9b1d03147bbfce54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:25:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Warden: fix live block-count reset + notate feed
 dedup/overlap (items 1 & 3)

ITEM 1 - 'block count doesn't track actual blocks' (field v2.1.2). Root cause:
'total blocked' is read from the live RW_DROP DROP-rule packet counter, but
apply.sh does 'iptables -N RW_DROP; -F RW_DROP' on every run AND re-runs on every
restart_firewall (firewall.c:9405 re-execs apply.sh directly) -> the counter was
zeroed on routine firewall restarts, so the UI total never accumulated. Fix:
apply.sh now snapshots the counter about to be flushed into a persisted /tmp
baseline (RW_BASE, accumulating) BEFORE teardown; stats.sh reports baseline +
live. Survives restart_firewall (which re-execs apply.sh, not start_rwarden);
resets only on a deliberate Warden reconfigure/disable (stop_rwarden unlinks
RW_BASE) or reboot (/tmp clears) - a live 'since this Warden session' total.
Read-only awk + one /tmp write before teardown: ZERO enforcement impact.
KNOWN RESIDUAL (metal-only, flagged in-code): does not recover drops the HW
flow-accelerator may offload without touching iptables.

ITEM 3 - feed dedup/overlap disclosure. New dict token RWDN_55 (all 25 dicts,
6189->6190 lockstep) under the feed checkboxes AND as a 'How Warden works'
bullet: all enabled feeds merge into ONE de-duplicated hash:net set (sort -u ->
ipset restore -> atomic swap), so overlapping feeds never double-block or bloat
matching; FireHOL Level 1 already aggregates Spamhaus DROP / DShield / Feodo
(Spamhaus still adds its IPv6 list). Addresses the 'feeds are duplicates' report.

NOT BUILT - rides a future rung; METAL OWED.
